per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.cor-cd-remaining"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.cor-cd-remaining"],"id":"long.cor-cd-remaining","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Corollary 10.7 (Only $`C_D\\in\\{-2,-1\\}`$ remain among the exceptional dyadic cells)","locator":"Long record Corollary 10.7, p. 116, label cor:cd-remaining","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*At a final middle row $D\\ge13$, Theorem 10.6 removes $-3$ from the exceptional set $\\{-3,-2,-1\\}$, leaving $-2,-1$ *within that set*. It does not assert $C_D\\in\\{-2,-1\\}$: nonnegative values have not been excluded. Proposition 10.5 handles upper transitions in the two-sided induction; it supplies no additional restriction on a middle coordinate. For the all-middle-row induction, the exclusion of all three values still needs proof without an all-right-tail assumption, together with the separate right-branch inequality.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.cor-cd-remaining","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.cor-cd-remaining","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.cor-cd-remaining%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_remaining_cells%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.cor-cd-remaining%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_remaining_cells%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_final_middle_cell_remaining_cells"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256: